 2. 🌊 House Dems clinch historic 258 seats 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Ballotpedia . Chart: Axios Visuals With 258 seats and counting, Democrats have clinched the biggest House majority for either party since the early 1990s .

 Democrats hit that number yesterday after North Carolina Democrat Chuck Hubbard defeated Republican Rep. Virginia Foxx, chair of the powerful Rules Committee. ( Go deeper ) Four races remain uncalled : Democrats lead by fewer than 350 votes in Minnesota's 1st District and Tennessee's 4th District. Two Louisiana races are headed to runoffs next month. 🔭 Zoom in: Democrats will hold at least as many seats as they did after Bill Clinton's first win in 1992, and more than the 257 they won when Barack Obama was elected in 2008.

 Their current margin over Republicans — 85 seats — is the widest for either party since 1990 (charted above). Go deeper . 

 
 
