 4. 💰 Charted: AI forecast freeze 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet. Chart: Matt Phillips/Axios Wall Street's spending forecasts for some of the AI boom's biggest players — Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft, Meta and Oracle — have leveled off, Axios' Matt Phillips writes. 

 Why it matters: Beyond the tech giants, the AI building spree has boosted profits at "picks-and-shovels" companies such as power providers and cable suppliers. Their stocks have delivered some of the buildout's most astonishing gains. AI investment has driven S&amp;P 500 earnings growth and overall corporate profitability to remarkably high levels.

