 5. 🇨🇦 Behind the scenes: Hegseth&#x27;s shot at Canada 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth speaks to the media last week in Caracas, Venezuela. Photo: Leonardo Fernández Viloria/Reuters Axios White House reporter Marc Caputo writes: 

 The Pentagon accused Canada of failing to become a "credible partner" due to its faltering military readiness and low defense spending, according to a sharply worded fact sheet issued by the Pentagon to justify new restrictions on America's northern neighbor.

 Why it matters: The restrictions deepen tensions between the U.S. and Canada over trade and defense, as Ottawa reconsiders billions of dollars in purchases of American weapons. The new restraints — which don't affect defense or intelligence sharing — limit fraternization by U.S. military personnel with their Canadian counterparts at official events without prior authorization from the Pentagon, an official told Axios. 

