 7. 🏛️ Snapshot: TrumpCare tease 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Image : Truth Social Sen.-elect Abdul El-Sayed (D-Mich.) is pitching President Trump on what El-Sayed branded "TrumpCare": a Medicare for All plan — gold insurance cards included — if he works with Democrats to pass it.

 Nine days after El-Sayed posted the images on X (13 million views), Trump shared an image of El-Sayed's tweet on Truth Social without comment. El-Sayed doubled down yesterday on NBC's "Meet the Press," saying he doesn't care what the plan is called and that if Trump wants a lasting legacy, "there is nothing better than the ultimate Trump card." 🥊 Reality check: An earlier White House statement blasted El-Sayed's plan, calling it "Medicare for None."

 
 
